  "output": {
    "answer": "That question isn't really answered in the record — everything documented was one setup, mine, running lanes solo. What is in the record is that the roles themselves are already separate, not fused: the gate is written before a run, review is done by a stronger model one tier up, and only a human — not a lane — flips the production flag, explicitly, never as a side effect. I did see that split in practice once, where a coordinator built a change and I made the actual flip decision myself. But scaling that pattern across several people isn't something the record covers.",
